# Every pattern here is ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading slash, on purpose.
#
# An unanchored pattern matches at any depth. `scripts/` excluded the repo's own
# scripts AND frontend/scripts, which deleted bundle-results.mjs and broke the
# site's prebuild step with "Cannot find module". That only appeared once the
# projects were connected to Git: a CLI deploy run from inside frontend/ never
# reads this file at all, so the two paths disagreed silently.

# Keep pyproject.toml out of Vercel builds.
#
# Neither project needs it: the API entry point puts src on sys.path rather than
# installing the package, and the frontend build reads results/full. Its
# presence, though, makes Vercel's Python builder switch to `uv lock`, which then
# fails because this project pins requires-python to >=3.11,<3.12 while the
# Vercel runtime is CPython 3.12. Excluding it keeps the builder on pip and
# requirements.txt -- the dependency set that was measured and tested.
/pyproject.toml

# Not needed by either deployed project.
/.venv/
/tests/
/docs/
/presentation/
/deploy/
/scripts/
/.superpowers/
